ing, screenwriting, cinematography, or another area of film.\n\n3. **Skills Transfer:** Highlight how skills from his computer science background, such as technical proficiency, problem-solving, and analytical thinking, can be valuable in the film industry, particularly in areas like visual effects or digital media.\n\n4. **Exposure and Experience:** Encourage Steven to gain practical experience in film through workshops, clubs, or part-time work to confirm his interest and build a portfolio.\n\n5. **Gradual Transition:** If possible, suggest taking a few film courses alongside his current studies to ease the transition and ensure this is the right path for him.\n\nBy focusing on their individual strengths and aspirations, the counselor can help both Nancy and Steven make informed decisions that align with their long-term goals and interests."}
