m his leadership style and gain insights into proactive behaviors.\n\n3. **Incremental Challenges:** Gradually increase the complexity of tasks assigned to Mary to build her confidence and demonstrate her ability to handle more responsibility.\n\n4. **Encouragement and Support:** Provide positive reinforcement and be patient with her progress. Regular check-ins and encouragement can boost her morale and help her feel more secure in her role.\n\n5. **Skill Development:** Identify specific areas where Mary needs additional training or development, and provide resources such as workshops, courses, or hands-on experiences to help her grow.\n\nBy leveraging Williams' assertiveness and leadership skills, and providing Mary with the support and training she needs, you can create a balanced and productive working environment for both interns. This approach not only helps them develop professionally but also contributes positively to the team's overall performance."}
